`ifndef HISI_I2C_DW_RDL
`define HISI_I2C_DW_RDL

regfile eHISI_I2C_DW {
    name = "HiSilicon I2C Master Controller (DesignWare-style register map)";
    desc = "
    HiSilicon master-only I2C controller of the Hi3518E V20X / Hi3516C V200 (data sheet issue 02, section 12.1). Three instances: I2C0 0x200D0000, I2C1 0x20240000, I2C2 0x20250000
    (all three share interrupt line 20 of the VIC, data sheet Table 3-8 `I2C0/I2C1/I2C2`). **Register layout is Synopsys-DesignWare-like** (I2C_CON, I2C_TAR, I2C_DATA_CMD, I2C_SCL_HCNT/LCNT, I2C_INTR_*,
    I2C_ENABLE, I2C_STATUS, TXFLR/RXFLR, SDA_HOLD, TX_ABRT_SRC, DMA_CR/TDLR/RDLR) with HiSilicon extensions: I2C_LOCK (0xAC, **locked at reset**), I2C_SCL_SWITCH / I2C_SCL_SIM (bus-recovery,
    \"anti-suspend\"), a single-register-access engine (I2C_MST_SINGLE_CTRL/CMD) and a DMA-driven sequential-read/write engine (I2C_SEQUENCE_CMD0..2). It is **not** the Hi3520D
    APB I2C (`eHISI_I2C`, different register map) and **not** the register layout implemented by the mainline `i2c-hibvt` driver (GLB at 0x0, SCL_H at 0x4, command FIFO at 0x30,
    compatibles `hisilicon,hibvt-i2c` / `hi3516cv300-i2c`): the Hi3518EV200 data sheet documents a different layout, and the vendor device tree for this SoC uses the out-of-tree
    compatible `hisilicon,hisi-i2c-hisilicon` for which no driver source is in the tree. FIFO depth: TXFLR/RXFLR are 5 bits (up to 16 or 32 entries).

    The same register map is in the Hi3516A/Hi3516D V100 data sheet (13.1, three instances, all 28 registers identical incl. resets) and, with differences, in the Hi3516A V200 (12.1)
    and Hi3519 V101 (12.1) data sheets: those two add I2C_CON[31] `i2c_mode_sel` and a second, \"non-standard timing mode\" register set MODE2_I2C_* at 0x800..0x81C that is
    the old HiSilicon APB I2C (`eHISI_I2C`: CTRL, COM, ICR, SR, SCL_H, SCL_L, TXR, RXR), and they do not document I2C_RX_TL, I2C_TX_TL, I2C_TXFLR, I2C_RXFLR, I2C_SCL_SWITCH and
    I2C_SCL_SIM (kept here; the registers are part of the DesignWare core and the SCL ones are HiSilicon additions documented for the other chips - unverified on those two chips).
    Both additions are enabled by the chip macro `I2C_DW_MODE2`. The Hi3516A V200 / Hi3519 reference clock is 49.5 MHz (MODE2_I2C_SCL_H/L formulas), Hi3516A V100 / Hi3518E V20X
    24 MHz. Not the Hi3511/Hi3515/Hi3520 V100 controller either: that is a plain 16-bit DesignWare DW_apb_i2c (`eDW_APB_I2C`).

    Scripted cross-chip audit 2026-11-11 (docs/rdl-campaign/i2c.md): the Hi3518E V20X / Hi3516C V200 and Hi3516A/D V100 data sheets agree with this block in every offset, field range, access and reset
    (differences are only field-name spellings and the `WC` write-clear bits of I2C_MST_SINGLE_CTRL, modelled `woclr`). The Hi3516A V200 / Hi3519 V101 data sheets print as reserved (RO 0) several bits that
    this block keeps from the other generation (Source: Hi3518E V20X data sheet, not confirmed for the two chips): I2C_INTR_STAT / I2C_INTR_MASK / I2C_INTR_RAW bits [8] and [4:0] (activity, tx_empty, tx_over,
    rx_full, rx_over, rx_under), I2C_STATUS bits [4:0] (only mst_activity [5] is printed; total reset 0x6 as in the block), I2C_TX_ABRT_SRC bits [9], [5], [4] (sbyte_norstrt, gcall_read, gcall_noack). The data
    sheets of those two chips also name the interrupt fields gen_call_int / start_det_int / stop_det_int / tx_abrt_int (STAT), stop_det_mask / tx_abrt_mask (MASK), *_raw_int (RAW); the Hi3516A V100 data sheet names
    I2C_SCL_HCNT[15:0] `i2c_fs_scl_hcnt`. Names here follow the Hi3518E V20X data sheet.

    | SoC | Instances | Base addresses | Interrupt |
    |-----|-----------|----------------|-----------|
    | Hi3516A / Hi3516D V100 | I2C0, I2C1, I2C2 | 0x200D0000, 0x20240000, 0x20250000 | GIC 46 (I2C0), 89 (I2C1), 90 (I2C2) |
    | Hi3518E V20X / Hi3516C V200 | I2C0, I2C1, I2C2 | 0x200D0000, 0x20240000, 0x20250000 | VIC 20 (shared) |
    | Hi3516A V200 / Hi3519 V101 (`I2C_DW_MODE2`) | I2C0-3 | 0x12110000 + n x 0x1000 | GIC 41 (SSP0/I2C0), 42 (SSP1/I2C1), 46 (I2C2), 44 (SSP3/I2C3) |

    Clocking (DS 12.1.2, 3.2.5): the I2C reference clock is 24 MHz in the data sheet's examples; the CRG selects it with PERI_CRG57 `i2c_cksel` [27:26] (00 = APB clock (reset default), 01 = 24 MHz,
    1x = 6 MHz) and the soft resets are PERI_CRG57 `i2c0_srst_req` [23], `i2c1_srst_req` [24], `i2c2_srst_req` [25]; there is no separate clock-gate bit. DMA request lines: I2C0 RX/TX = 0/1, I2C1 = 2/3,
    I2C2 = 10/11 (DMAC Table 3-12). The data register for DMA is the I2C_DATA_CMD at +0x10.

    SCL timing (DS I2C_SCL_HCNT/LCNT): counts are in units of the reference clock; standard mode count = (fi2c/fSCL) x 0.5 each, fast mode HCNT = 0.36 x and LCNT = 0.64 x (fi2c/fSCL).

    All registers are 32 bits wide; unlisted upper bits are reserved. Register layout, resets and bit descriptions are from the data sheet 12.1.5 (`hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` lines 77731-79299); the
    bit descriptions are the data sheet's text. There is no vendor driver for this layout in the source trees, so nothing here is cross-checked against code or hardware.
    ";


    reg {
        name = "I2C control register";
        desc = "I2C_CON is an I2C control register.

Total reset value 0x65: bit 5 `restart_en` resets to 1; bits 6, 2 and 0 are listed as reserved by the data sheet but read 1 at reset (modelled as `reserved_b*` so that the register total matches the data sheet). The data sheet does not describe a master-enable / speed / slave-disable field in this register (unlike a Synopsys DesignWare IC_CON); master mode is implicit. **All registers except I2C_LOCK are write-protected after reset, see I2C_LOCK.**

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_CON (offset 0x0, printed page 12-5, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 77797).";

`ifdef I2C_DW_MODE2
        enum I2C_CON_i2c_mode_sel_enum {
            STANDARD_TIMING = 0 { name = "Standard Timing"; desc = "standard timing mode (the DesignWare-style registers below)"; };
            NON_STANDARD_TIMING = 1 { name = "Non-standard Timing"; desc = "non-standard timing mode (the MODE2_I2C_* registers at 0x800..0x81C)"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "i2c_mode_sel";
            desc = "I2C mode select (Hi3516A V200 / Hi3519 V101 data sheet I2C_CON[31]).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_CON_i2c_mode_sel_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } i2c_mode_sel[31:31];

`endif
        field {
            name = "reserved_b6";
            desc = "Reserved. The data sheet lists this bit as RO reserved but its total reset value 0x0000_0065 has this bit set (reads 1 at reset).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_b6[6:6];

        enum I2C_CON_restart_en_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED_IF_RESTART = 1 { name = "Enabled If Restart"; desc = "enabled If the Restart function is disabled, the following functions are not supported: sending the start bit, high-speed mode, read operation in 10-bit addressing mode, combined addressing mode."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "restart_en";
            desc = "Restart command TX enable in master mode";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_CON_restart_en_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } restart_en[5:5];

        field {
            name = "reserved_b2";
            desc = "Reserved. The data sheet lists this bit as RO reserved but its total reset value 0x0000_0065 has this bit set (reads 1 at reset).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_b2[2:2];

        field {
            name = "reserved_b0";
            desc = "Reserved. The data sheet lists this bit as RO reserved but its total reset value 0x0000_0065 has this bit set (reads 1 at reset).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_b0[0:0];
    } I2C_CON @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "I2C access slave device address register";
        desc = "I2C_TAR is an I2C access slave device address register.

Reset 0x2C is the data sheet value (7-bit address 0x2C, not a typical sensor address).

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_TAR (offset 0x4, printed page 12-6, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 77839).";

        enum I2C_TAR_master_10bit_enum {
            V_7_BITS = 0 { name = "V 7 Bits"; desc = "7 bits"; };
            V_10_BITS = 1 { name = "V 10 Bits"; desc = "10 bits"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "master_10bit";
            desc = "Address length in master mode";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_TAR_master_10bit_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } master_10bit[12:12];

        enum I2C_TAR_special_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "special";
            desc = "General call or start byte function enable";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_TAR_special_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } special[11:11];

        enum I2C_TAR_gc_or_start_enum {
            GENERAL_CALL_COMMAND = 0 { name = "General Call Command"; desc = "general call command (After the general call command is sent, you can perform only write operations. If you perform read operations, tx_abort interrupt is triggered. For details about the definition.)"; };
            START_BYTE_COMMAND = 1 { name = "Start Byte Command"; desc = "start byte command"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "gc_or_start";
            desc = "I2C command to be executed when the Special bit is 1";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_TAR_gc_or_start_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } gc_or_start[10:10];

        field {
            name = "i2c_tar";
            desc = "Slave address that is accessed by the I2C when I2C acts as a master device";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2C;
        } i2c_tar[9:0];
    } I2C_TAR @ 0x4;

    reg {
        name = "I2C data operation register";
        desc = "I2C_DATA_CMD is an I2C data operation register.

The data sheet lists bit 8 as reserved: there is no read/write command bit (a DesignWare IC_DATA_CMD has CMD at bit 8); read and write transfers are driven through the I2C_MST_SINGLE_* / I2C_SEQUENCE_CMD* registers or, in this DS flow chart, through the FIFO with the command implied. The data sheet gives no worked example of a plain FIFO read, and no vendor driver source for this IP is in the tree: behaviour of the FIFO path is data-sheet only.

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_DATA_CMD (offset 0x10, printed page 12-7, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 77893).";

        field {
            name = "data";
            desc = "Data to be transmitted or received through the I2C bus Read: The data received from the I2C bus is read. Write: The written data is transmitted to the I2C.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } data[7:0];
    } I2C_DATA_CMD @ 0x10;

    reg {
        name = "I2C_SCL high level configuration register";
        desc = "I2C_SCL_HCNT is an I2C_SCL high level configuration register.

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_SCL_HCNT (offset 0x1C, printed page 12-7, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 77920).";

        field {
            name = "i2c_scl_hcnt";
            desc = "High-level time of the SCL clock. The timing unit is I2C working reference clock (24 MHz is used as an example). It is recommended that the field value be 1/2 of the SCL clock cycle in standard mode and be 0.36 of the SCL clock in fast mode. That is, i2c_scl_hcnt is calculated as follows: In standard mode: i2c_scl_hcnt = (fi2c/fSCL) x 0.5 In fast mode: i2c_scl_hcnt = (fi2c/fSCL) x 0.36 For example, if the 400 kHz SCL clock works in fast mode, i2c_scl_hcnt is 22 (0.36 x 24 MHz/400 kHz).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x10;
        } i2c_scl_hcnt[15:0];
    } I2C_SCL_HCNT @ 0x1C;

    reg {
        name = "I2C_SCL low level configuration register";
        desc = "I2C_SCL_LCNT is an I2C_SCL low level configuration register.

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_SCL_LCNT (offset 0x20, printed page 12-8, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 77962).";

        field {
            name = "i2c_scl_lcnt";
            desc = "Low-level time of the SCL clock. The timing unit is I2C working reference clock (24 MHz is used as an example). It is recommended that the field value be 1/2 of the SCL clock cycle in standard mode and be 0.64 of the SCL clock in fast mode. That is, i2c_scl_lcnt is calculated as follows: In standard mode: i2c_scl_lcnt = (fi2c/fSCL) x 0.5 In fast mode: i2c_scl_lcnt = (fi2c/fSCL) x 0.64 For example, if the 400 kHz SCL clock works in fast mode, i2c_scl_lcnt is 38 (0.64 x 24 MHz/400 kHz).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x10;
        } i2c_scl_lcnt[15:0];
    } I2C_SCL_LCNT @ 0x20;

    reg {
        name = "I2C masked interrupt status register";
        desc = "I2C_INTR_STAT is an interrupt status register after the I2C is masked.

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_INTR_STAT (offset 0x2C, printed page 12-9, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 78006).";

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_gen_call_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "gen_call";
            desc = "Status of the interrupt indicating that a general call request is received";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_gen_call_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } gen_call[11:11];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_start_det_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "start_det";
            desc = "Status of the start detect interrupt indicating the I2C bus interface has the START or RESTART condition";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_start_det_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } start_det[10:10];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_stop_det_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "stop_det";
            desc = "Status of the start detect interrupt indicating the I2C bus interface has the STOP condition";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_stop_det_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } stop_det[9:9];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_activity_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "activity";
            desc = "Activity interrupt status. The I2C activity status is recorded until the interrupt is cleared.";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_activity_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } activity[8:8];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_tx_abrt_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_abrt";
            desc = "TX abort interrupt status";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_tx_abrt_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } tx_abrt[6:6];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_tx_empty_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_empty";
            desc = "Status of the interrupt indicating that TX_FIFO reaches or is below the threshold";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_tx_empty_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } tx_empty[4:4];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_tx_over_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_over";
            desc = "TX_FIFO overflow interrupt status";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_tx_over_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } tx_over[3:3];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_rx_full_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_full";
            desc = "Status of the interrupt indicating that RX_FIFO reaches or is above the threshold";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_rx_full_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rx_full[2:2];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_rx_over_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_over";
            desc = "RX_FIFO overflow interrupt status";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_rx_over_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rx_over[1:1];

        enum I2C_INTR_STAT_rx_under_enum {
            NO_INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 0 { name = "No Interrupt Generated"; desc = "No interrupt is generated."; };
            INTERRUPT_GENERATED = 1 { name = "Interrupt Generated"; desc = "An interrupt is generated."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_under";
            desc = "Read data overflow (that is, the CPU reads the FIFO when RX_FIFO is empty) interrupt status";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            encode = I2C_INTR_STAT_rx_under_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rx_under[0:0];
    } I2C_INTR_STAT @ 0x2C;

    reg {
        name = "I2C interrupt mask register";
        desc = "I2C_INTR_MASK is an I2C interrupt mask register.

Polarity as printed in the data sheet (1 = masked). A Synopsys DesignWare IC_INTR_MASK has the opposite polarity (1 = not masked); the data sheet text was kept because no hardware access or vendor driver is available; check on hardware.

Data sheet 12.1.5 I2C_INTR_MASK (offset 0x30, printed page 12-10, `hi3518ev200--Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 78087).";

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_gen_call_mask_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "gen_call_mask";
            desc = "Interrupt mask when a general call request is received";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_gen_call_mask_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } gen_call_mask[11:11];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_start_det_mask_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "start_det_mask";
            desc = "Start detect interrupt mask";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_start_det_mask_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } start_det_mask[10:10];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_stop_det_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "stop_det";
            desc = "Stop detect interrupt mask";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_stop_det_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } stop_det[9:9];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_activity_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "activity";
            desc = "Activity interrupt mask";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_activity_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } activity[8:8];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_tx_abrt_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_abrt";
            desc = "TX abort interrupt mask";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_tx_abrt_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } tx_abrt[6:6];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_tx_empty_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_empty";
            desc = "Interrupt mask when TX_FIFO reaches or is below the threshold";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_tx_empty_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } tx_empty[4:4];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_tx_over_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "tx_over";
            desc = "TX_FIFO overflow interrupt mask";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_tx_over_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } tx_over[3:3];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_rx_full_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_full";
            desc = "Interrupt mask when RX_FIFO reaches or is below the threshold";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_rx_full_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rx_full[2:2];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_rx_over_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "rx_over";
            desc = "RX_FIFO overflow interrupt mask";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = I2C_INTR_MASK_rx_over_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rx_over[1:1];

        enum I2C_INTR_MASK_rx_under_enum {
            NOT_MASKED = 0 { name = "Not Masked"; desc = "not masked"; };
            MASKED = 1 { name = "Masked"; desc = "masked"; };
        };

